1
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Israel, 1973... One woman stood between victory and defeat.

2
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Golda is a drama, history, war film directed by Guy Nattiv.

3
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Set during the tense 19 days of the Yom Kippur War in 1973, Israeli Prime Minister
Golda Meir is faced with the potential of Israel’s complete destruction.

4
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
She must navigate overwhelming odds, a skeptical cabinet and a complex relationship with US
Secretary of State Henry Kissinger, with millions of lives in the balance.

5
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Her tough leadership and compassion would ultimately decide the fate of her
nation and leave her with a controversial legacy around the world.

6
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Golda Meir, played by Helen Mirren.

7
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Lou Kaddar, played by Camille Cottin.

8
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Henry Kissinger, played by Liev Schreiber.

9
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:33,000
David 'Dado' Elazar, played by Lior Ashkenazi.

10
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Moshe Dayan, played by Rami Heuberger.

11
00:55:33,000 --> 00:55:39,000
Zvi Zamir, played by Rotem Keinan.

12
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
Golda is a 2023 biographical drama film directed by Guy
Nattiv and written by Nicholas Martin.

13
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:45,000
The film depicts the actions of Golda Meir, the 4th Prime
Minister of Israel, during the Yom Kippur War.

14
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
It stars Helen Mirren, Camille Cottin and Liev Schreiber.

15
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
It received its world premiere at the 2023 Berlin
International Film Festival on February 20, 2023.

16
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It was released in the United States by Bleecker Street and Shivhans Pictures on August 25, 2023, and in the
United Kingdom and Ireland by Vertical Entertainment and MetFilm Distribution on October 6, 2023.

17
01:25:51,000 --> 01:25:57,000
The film received a Best Makeup and Hairstyling
nomination at the 96th Academy Awards.

18
01:30:54,000 --> 01:31:00,000
The film explores themes of israel, zionism, based on
true story, political leader, occupation.

19
01:35:57,000 --> 01:36:03,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
